# Content Orchestrator Engineering Standard

This rule applies to **every task** in this repository. Skills under
`.cursor/skills/` specialize roles; this rule is a non-negotiable baseline.

**Priority:** Subordinate to the **CEO Master Rule**
(`.cursor/rules/ceo-master-rule.mdc`). On conflict, CEO Master Rule wins
unless the Founder explicitly approves an exception.

## Architecture

- Follow the **approved architecture** and stack: FastAPI, **SQLAlchemy 2.x**,
  **Alembic**, **PostgreSQL** (source of truth), React + TypeScript, Python workers.
- **Never introduce architecture drift** (no alternate SoT, ORM, queue-as-SoT,
  or second orchestration engine without an accepted ADR + `/ceo`).
- Prefer **existing project patterns** over inventing new ones.
- Keep implementations **simple, maintainable, and production-ready**.
- Protect **backward compatibility** unless an **approved migration plan** exists.
- Architecture changes require documentation (`/documentation-writer` /
  `/chief-architect` as applicable).

## Non-negotiable product controls

- **Human Review Gate** is mandatory — no bypass paths.
- **Spend controls** are mandatory — no “just run it” around caps/reservations.
- **Workspace isolation** is mandatory — tenant data stays workspace-scoped.
- **FORCE RLS** is mandatory on tenant-owned tables — app filters alone are insufficient.
- **PostgreSQL** is the orchestration **source of truth**.

## Schema & migrations

- Use **SQLAlchemy 2.x** for models/queries.
- Use **Alembic for all schema changes** — no ad-hoc production DDL as SoT.
- **All migrations must be reversible** (or an explicit expand/contract +
  forward-fix plan approved by `/postgresql-expert` and accepted by `/ceo`).

## Quality bar

- **No TODOs** on in-scope production paths claimed complete.
- **No placeholders** or mock success presented as production behavior.
- **No silent failures** — errors must surface; no swallowed exceptions that drop work.
- Every feature requires **comprehensive tests** (real PostgreSQL for API/DB behavior).

## Independent verification (mandatory)

- Every **security-sensitive** change requires **`/security-auditor`** review.
- Every implementation requires **`/qa-breaker`** review before release claims.
- Every release requires **`/release-manager`** approval (readiness evidence).
- **Never merge** without independent verification (human order + QA + security).
- **Never claim VERIFIED** without **factual evidence** (CI URL + SHA, tests,
  migration head, specialist reports as applicable).

